        {
          "id": 1634456932,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Hi @alagoutte, in this case, its a copy/paste from 4 items ago.  check_typed_item_calls.py could have warned in 2 ways:\n\n- if they were actually consecutive, which in this case they are not.  I could widen the search here to a few (rather than just 1) above?  I do sometimes add (say) 5 items at the same time with a copy and paste, then edit each one\n\n- the label_vs_filter check if > 93% of filters match the labels (with some fixup rules).  There are 78 cases (75%) in that dissector that don't match, so that'd be too many entries to look through",
          "author": {
            "id": 6810036,
            "username": "martin.r.mathieson",
